    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, doc, what brings me in is that since I retired—I used to be in construction, you know, framing houses mostly. Good work, honest work. But since I stopped working, I can’t seem to slow down. I’m up and moving from one little job to the next all day long, like I still have a crew waiting on me. My wife says I'm wearing a groove in the floorboards. Speaking of floorboards, we had to replace the ones in the hallway last summer because of a leak from the old water heater. Took me three days to get the matching oak, had to drive all the way out to a lumber yard in the next county. But yeah, I just can't seem to sit still anymore.",
