    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from being physically active, have you noticed your mood feeling unusually high, elated, or irritable lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "High or irritable? No, I wouldn't say that. My mood is just... my normal mood, you know? I mean, sure, I get a little cranky if I can't find my tools in the garage. Like the other day, my grandson came over and borrowed my good tape measure. He’s trying to build a birdhouse. Nice kid, really, but he doesn't know the first thing about woodworking. I had to tell him, you gotta measure twice and cut once. That's what my first boss, Old Man Peterson, drilled into my head back in '77. \n\nPeterson was a tough guy. He was actually missing half his left index finger from a table saw accident. He never talked about it, but we all knew. You had to be real careful around those old saws, they didn't have all the fancy automatic safety guards and sensors they do now. You just had to pay attention or you'd lose a digit. Anyway, Peterson would always... wait, what did you ask me? Something about feeling high or angry? \n\nNo, no, nothing like that. I'm not walking around mad at the world or feeling like I'm on top of it, either. Just normal, I guess. Just can't stop moving.",
